{"availability":"available","full":"arcanite24/pinyon-shift","name":"pinyon-shift","description":"A playable preview of Forza Horizon static recompilation","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":347,"forks":16,"created":"2026-08-25T21:37:12Z","updated":"2026-10-11T05:06:36Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://arcanite24.github.io/pinyon-shift/","topics":["forza-horizon","rexglue","static-recompilation","windows","xbox-360"],"demo":"https://arcanite24.github.io/pinyon-shift/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:52.788Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:52.788Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:52.788Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:52.788Z","stars":347,"forks":16}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Xbox 360 release of Forza Horizon, recompiled to run natively on Windows.","Built on your own PC from your own disc, with internal resolutions up to 4K.","Pinyon Shift is not an emulator. The game's PowerPC code is translated ahead of time into C++ with ShiftGlue, our fork of ReXGlue, and compiled for x86-64 on your computer. The GPU command stream the game builds is executed by a native renderer written for Forza Horizon, on Vulkan (the default) or Direct3D 12. The project is a playable preview: early, imperfect, and surprisingly drivable."],"features":["Native code. The title's executable is recompiled ahead of time; nothing","is interpreted or JIT-compiled at run time.","A renderer built for this game. Every draw, clear, resolve and swap runs","in order with the game's own shaders, translated to SPIR-V (Vulkan) or DXBC (Direct3D 12). On Vulkan, one thread decodes the game's command stream while a second records the draws.","60 and 120 fps at the right game speed. The render rate is decoupled from"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/arcanite24/pinyon-shift/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"763041ae597360a26dba46e2c9add633fe8a4ee8148c555bb12545b110d30b70","ex